uth-gateway, and topology.json lists AUTH-2026-0318 as a recent auth-gateway change just before the incident.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"excluded_red_herrings\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"signal\\\": \\\"orders-db CPU spike\\\",\\n      \\\"why_not_primary\\\": \\\"orders-db latency stayed normal, errors stayed at 0, and both payment-api and orders-db logs say failing checkout requests did not reach the database path before the auth gate failed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"signal\\\": \\\"cdn-edge 5xx errors\\\",\\n      \\\"why_not_primary\\\": \\\"Metrics say the CDN issue was isolated to static images, and checkout-web logs say static assets served normally after retry while checkout remained blocked by auth failures.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"signal\\\": \\\"DB-2026-0144 recent change\\\",\\n      \\\"why_not_primary\\\": \\\"topology.json marks the orders-db change as vacuum tuning only with no schema or credential change, and observed DB behavior remained healthy during the incident.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"recommended_next_steps\\\": [\\n    \\\"Mitigate now by restoring auth-gateway allowed_issuers/JWKS namespace support for partner-v2 or rolling back AUTH-2026-0318.\\\",\\n    \\\"Verify after mitigation that auth-gateway stops logging issuer_not_allowed for token_issuer=partner-v2.\\\",\\n    \\\"Verify payment-api create_payment requests no longer fail with auth_result=invalid_issuer and that checkout-web 401 rates return to baseline.\\\",\\n    \\\"Add a deployment guard that checks issuer and allowed_issuers parity for partner-token validation before auth-gateway rollout.\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"}"}}
